{
  "id": "fluid_flow___euler_equations",
  "title": "Fluid Flow - Euler Equations",
  "description": "The behavior of ideal compressible gas can be described with Euler equations. The Euler Equations govern the motion of compressible, inviscid fluids.",
  "type": "calculator-chart",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Euler Equations for Compressible Fluid Flow\n\nThe Euler equations describe the motion of ideal compressible fluids without viscosity. These conservation equations form the foundation for understanding gas dynamics and fluid behavior.\n\n### Key Equations:\n\n**Conservation of Mass (Continuity Equation):**\n$$\\frac{\\partial \\rho}{\\partial t} + \\nabla \\cdot (\\rho \\mathbf{v}) = 0$$\n\n**Conservation of Momentum:**\n$$\\frac{\\partial (\\rho \\mathbf{v})}{\\partial t} + \\nabla \\cdot (\\rho \\mathbf{v} \\otimes \\mathbf{v}) + \\nabla p = 0$$\n\n**Conservation of Energy:**\n$$\\frac{\\partial E}{\\partial t} + \\nabla \\cdot ((E + p)\\mathbf{v}) = 0$$\n\nWhere:\n- **ρ** = Density\n- **v** = Velocity vector\n- **p** = Pressure\n- **E** = Total energy per unit volume\n\n### Reference:\n[Euler Equations (Fluid Dynamics) - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euler_equations_\\(fluid_dynamics\\))"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "density",
          "label": "Density (ρ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 1.225
        },
        {
          "id": "velocity",
          "label": "Velocity (v)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "defaultValue": 10
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure",
          "label": "Pressure (p)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 101325
        },
        {
          "id": "gamma",
          "label": "Heat Capacity Ratio (γ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "defaultValue": 1.4
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "momentum",
          "label": "Momentum per Unit Volume",
          "unit": "kg/(m²·s)",
          "formula": "inputs.density * inputs.velocity",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "kinetic_energy",
          "label": "Kinetic Energy per Unit Volume",
          "unit": "J/m³",
          "formula": "0.5 * inputs.density * inputs.velocity * inputs.velocity",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "total_energy",
          "label": "Total Energy per Unit Volume (Internal + Kinetic)",
          "unit": "J/m³",
          "formula": "(inputs.pressure / (inputs.gamma - 1)) + (0.5 * inputs.density * inputs.velocity * inputs.velocity)",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "speed_of_sound",
          "label": "Speed of Sound",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "formula": "Math.sqrt(inputs.gamma * inputs.pressure / inputs.density)",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "mach_number",
          "label": "Mach Number",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "formula": "inputs.velocity / Math.sqrt(inputs.gamma * inputs.pressure / inputs.density)",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "chart",
      "headers": [
        "Flow Parameter",
        "Subsonic (M<1)",
        "Sonic (M=1)",
        "Supersonic (M>1)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Velocity Regime",
          "v < a",
          "v = a",
          "v > a"
        ],
        [
          "Mach Number Range",
          "0 - 1",
          "1",
          "1+"
        ],
        [
          "Compressibility Effects",
          "Weak",
          "Critical",
          "Strong"
        ],
        [
          "Shock Formation",
          "None",
          "Critical",
          "Present"
        ],
        [
          "Flow Behavior",
          "Streamlines Smooth",
          "Transition Zone",
          "Complex Patterns"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}